This code checks for `arr[i] >= arr[i+1]` — meaning the current element is >= the next one. When this happens, it records `i` (the index of the *first* element in the descending pair) as a candidate.

But the problem asks for the **largest index of an element which is not greater than or equal to the element immediately preceding it** — that is, we want the largest `j` such that `arr[j] <= arr[j-1]`. So the candidate index should be `j = i+1`, not `i`.

